  "item": [
    {
      "id": "fdee4d69-1744-43ad-80c0-db18be57a8cc",
      "name": "TemplateCustomFields",
      "description": {
        "content": "The TemplateCustomFields resource provides methods that allow you manage custom fields in an template. \n\nCustom fields can be used in the templates for your account to record information about the template, help search for templates and track information. The template custom fields are shown in the Template Settings section when a user is creating an template in the DocuSign member console. The template custom fields are not seen by the template recipients.\n\nThere are two types of template custom fields, text and list. A text custom field lets the sender enter the value for the field. With a list custom field, the sender selects the value of the field from a pre-made list.",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
